    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_362926ef4845314204ee0afbe2d72869da047900e5784a12094c1e9653b2c7d1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The ordinary/supersingular distinction is reliable only when geometric curve, finite base field, chosen Frobenius, endomorphisms after extension, and descent are not collapsed: structural diagnostics classify the curve, but changing or forgetting the base-field/Frobenius data changes the arithmetic situation and invalidates Hasse's claimed supersingular endpoint-trace converse.",
