    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_bbca378ae2a4f63a64f8e71396c00cc8698659d343d5c789f6f6e612457581c4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across Artin's finite coefficient polynomial, the all-extension point-count series, Schmidt's intrinsic rational curve zeta function, and Hasse's second elliptic proof, the source progressively relocates a zero-location problem into finite spectral data: point counts determine zeta coefficients, the curve numerator factors through Frobenius quantities, and the elliptic identity between Frobenius and its conjugate gives norm q and hence pRH.",
