    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_de8a69ec2591b21371cf6f5fdfcfc235fc735861305d9f7db1ac7be2238dbef1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source makes mathematical representation operational rather than merely terminological: Schmidt's intrinsic function-field language removes dependence on a chosen affine variable and separates the zeta problem's proved and open parts; Deuring's function-field correspondence ring supplies a higher-genus carrier but not the needed norm; Weil then identifies an equivalent Italian-geometric ring whose reusable ideas were difficult to translate across dialects. This concrete pRH episode instantiates the broader historical claim that the eventual proof mechanism, not an inherited disciplinary label, determines where RH or an avatar belongs.",
